Overlay patch 0031: iOS audio self-pump — THE sibling-wide "fuzzy audio
on thumb-press" fix (2ship overlay 0024 / PORTING-DELTAS.md, device-confirmed
across every port except SoH). Ghostship's HandleAudioThread is the OLD
coupled loop: a plain cv.wait() that produces one frame only on the game
loop's per-tick notify. On iOS the game loop IS the UIKit main thread, so a
pressed thumb's up-to-120 Hz touch events delay the notify past the ring's
headroom and the SDL backend drains to crackle. SoH is clean because upstream
evolved this exact loop (their clicks fix #6594): a 5 ms self-pump (wait_for),
a producer guard, and a pre-buffer reservoir. Ported __IOS__-gated (macOS
oracle keeps pristine upstream behavior), preserving Ghostship's
processing/cv_from_thread handshake and its master-volume + ModAudio_MixInto
production verbatim in produce_and_play.

DEGENERACY CHECK (mandatory per the deltas doc; it caught a shipped-quality
bug on 2ship): SoH's exact producer guard (Buffered + burst <= Desired)
COLLAPSES here — one production is ~1088 samples and DesiredBuffered is 1100
(≈ one burst), so it would only produce when nearly empty and the ring would
hit empty every cycle. Use the documented skip-when-above intent instead
(produce while Buffered <= Desired); overshoot is bounded to one burst, well
under the SDL backend's refusal. Instrumented: min/max backend-buffered
samples per window into atomics the 0008 probe reports as aud_min/aud_max
(0 = underrun — the retest number). Coupled to 0008 (the probe reads the
atomics this patch defines); the series applies atomically. rev: audio-thread
QoS (USER_INTERACTIVE) so thermal pressure can't starve it.

--- a/src/port/Engine.cpp
+++ b/src/port/Engine.cpp
@@ -1215,11 +1215,109 @@
